
  
 Heap provides access to physical memory, Resources provide access to virtual memory
 

 Heap
   Part of pool (L0/L1/L2 : Sysmem, GPUMEM, UMA)
   
   :: Physical memory
   
   Type : Helps you optimize access patterns more efficiently https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/d3d12/ne-d3d12-d3d12_heap_type
     - Default	    : GPU Only (can't access from CPU)
     - Upload	    : Optimized for CPU writes (WC) and GPU read-once  (typically placed in sysmem)
     - Readback     : Optimized for CPU reads (WB) and  GPU write-once (typically placed in sysmem *I think*)
     - GPUupload    : BAR1 mapped to CPU
     

 Resource
    Type : Buffer, Texture, Sampler
    
    Views (Descriptors)
	SRV, UAV, CBV,
	Sampler,
	RTV/DSV

	IBV, VBV, SOV (Index Buffer, Vertex Buffer, Stream Output View)
	;; Descriptors can be allocated on descriptor heap
	
    :: Virtual memory
    - can call map/unmap based on underlying Heap to get CPU pointers

    ;; Types (CPR)
       Committed : Comes with committed Resource (VA) and Heap (PA)
       Placed    : Comes with VA but can be mapped to Heap PA dynamically.  (No Partial Residency)
       		   Allows layering many Resources on top of a single Heap lazily.
		   To move Placed Resources to another Heap, explicit copy and reinitialization of resource descriptors is required
       Reserved  : Comes with VA but can be mapped in parts to various Heap ranges (Partial Residency, think Texture Streaming)

